## CI topology
Build, tests, lint, architecture checks, coverage and review run centrally
from the hub through the `.github/workflows/agents.yml` stub; they do not
appear as workflow files here. Never create or modify files under
`.github/workflows/` to add CI. If a CI gap exists, raise it as a hub change
request (approved by the owner or approvers). App-level build config (linter
and architecture configs included) is allowed; it is app config, not CI.

## Branching
- Single-branch model: one long-lived branch, `__BRANCH__`. Agents branch
  from it (`agent/*`, `design/*`, short-lived) and open PRs against it.
  Merging into it may be a production release; there is no promotion step.
  If this section is blank, agents use the repository default branch.

